(* ===================================================================== *)
(* ConstructiveWorld-Main - calibwin small-step chain: assembling certificates at the window point n = 29 *)
(** * planb4_calib_chain_build_n29: poleA/poleB chain tails and the assembled abqA/abqB values for point 29, rewritten level by level from the block certificates: pb4cwin_poleAeq/poleBeq assemble the full pole literal from the step_n29 block certificates through pb4cwin_laur_go_split: the laur wrapper is unfolded and the block split is rewritten in, each block boundary is bridged by a remainder-state certificate (one 8-step pb4cwin_rem bite), the glue lemma rewrites the readout into segments, each segment collapses to its imported literal, and one small bite closes the map/nth readout.  pb4cwin_abqAeq/abqBeq rewrite the two pole arguments of planb4_rs/planb4_ss to their literals and bite only the residual assembly (witness scale, polynomial part, principal fold, Qred).  Boolean plq_eqb / Qeq_bool faces derive from the eq-face certificates.  Fold-window Examples cover the principal sums per window at Qred face, the deep-window insurance face.

    Mission.  poleA/poleB chain tails and the assembled abqA/abqB values for point 29, rewritten level by level from the block certificates: pb4cwin_poleAeq/poleBeq assemble the full pole literal from the step_n29 block certificates through pb4cwin_laur_go_split: the laur wrapper is unfolded and the block split is rewritten in, each block boundary is bridged by a remainder-state certificate (one 8-step pb4cwin_rem bite), the glue lemma rewrites the readout into segments, each segment collapses to its imported literal, and one small bite closes the map/nth readout.  pb4cwin_abqAeq/abqBeq rewrite the two pole arguments of planb4_rs/planb4_ss to their literals and bite only the residual assembly (witness scale, polynomial part, principal fold, Qred).  Boolean plq_eqb / Qeq_bool faces derive from the eq-face certificates.  Fold-window Examples cover the principal sums per window at Qred face, the deep-window insurance face.

    Dependencies.  zzm1_gauss (zzId, mkz, gz_im_neg_frac); zzm2_qpoly (plq_eqb); zzm1b_linform_bridge (zz_sumf); planb4_g1_laur_extract; planb4_g1_rs_channel (planb4_rs, planb4_ss); planb4_g1_ab_def (planb4_abqA, planb4_abqB); planb4_calib_chain_glue_qred (pb4cwin_zzId_eq); planb4_calib_chain_glue_laur (pb4cwin_laur_go_split, pb4cwin_rem); planb4_calib_chain_step_n29; stdlib QArith, ZArith, List.

    References.  piu_zz_tau_segtree_1024_merge.v:36-45 (change, glue rewrite, twin rewrite, small bite template); planb4_g1_ab_def.v:60-67 (the assemblies); planb4_g1_rs_channel.v:46-51 (rs/ss faces); planb3_g1_calib.v (the frozen A/B table rows the point literals transcribe).

    Constructivity.  Every assembling lemma is a real rewrite chain over the glue equations; the only bites are the imported per-block certificates, one remainder-state bridge bite per block boundary, plus one residual assembly bite per channel and per fold window; no axioms, no admits; every statement carries Print Assumptions.

    Build.  coqc -native-compiler no -time -q -Q <this sandbox> "" -Q <tree ConstructiveWorld_Live> "" planb4_calib_chain_build_n29.v (Rocq 9.3.0; cpu_guard_v3 wrapped; products stay in this sandbox, the module tree is read-only). *)

